00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:07.110 align:start position:0%
eu employment and social affairs  ministers have adopted a recommendation  on a quality framework for traineeships  the aim is to ensure an efficient  education to work transition increasing  young people's employability  traineeships should offer quality  learning content and adequate working  conditions to best help people find jobs  this recommendation along with other  initiatives the initiatives for youth  employment  for the guarantee for the youth  system will contribute in integrating  the young  in our labor market ministers have also  agreed to a proposal on a social summit  for growth and employment  during policy debate on the 2014  european semester exercise ministers  adopted the conclusions that constitute  their contribution to the meeting of eu  leaders in march they also adopted a  report on employment and agreed on the  guidelines of employment policy  furthermore a regulation on the fund for  aid to the most deprived has been  adopted  over the next seven years member states  will have 3.5 billion euros to provide  material assistance to people in need or  to use in social inclusion projects
 

